#!/root/kovanica-agent/venv/bin/python3
"""
Kovi CLI — command-line interface to the Kovanica engineering agent.

Wraps the agent's tools (code search, file read, cargo execution, patch
proposal) into a terminal workflow. The agent runs locally against the
protocol repo at /root/kovanica-protocol (REPOS_PATH), calling an OpenAI-
compatible LLM for reasoning and using the agent's tool set directly
instead of going through the FastAPI HTTP layer.

Usage:
  kovi chat "how is selected_parent computed"
  kovi explain mergeset
  kovi search "coinbase maturity"
  kovi cargo test -p kovanica-dag
  kovi kovanica head
  kovi diff crates/kovanica-state/src/ledger.rs "fix maturity" '--- a/...'

Environment:
  LLM_BASE_URL / VLLM_BASE_URL / Ollama : LLM endpoint (OpenAI chat protocol)
  LLM_API_KEY / XAI_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY : API key
  AGENT_MODEL : model name (default: qwen2.5-coder:3b on CPU, Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct-AWQ on GPU)
  KOVANICA_NODE_URL : read-only node RPC for /api/head (default: https://explorer.kovanica.online)
  REPOS_PATH : protocol repo root (default: /repos/kovanica-protocol -> /root/kovanica-protocol)

The LLM is an external inference service. Kovi provides the agent layer
(tools, grounding, safety rules). On CPU hosts the default model is
qwen2.5-coder:3b via Ollama; on GPU it is Qwen/Qwen2.5-Coder-32B-Instruct-AWQ via vLLM.

Safety rules (from SYSTEM_PROMPT.md, enforced in code):
  - Never run KOVANICA_OPERATOR=1 or any operator override
  - Never apply a patch to the real repo; only propose (git_diff_suggest semantics)
  - Only cargo check/test/clippy/build may run
  - Never write, log, or echo back secrets
  - Never invent file paths — cite real ones or say so
"""

